WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.150
This is Otto.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.428
Every coding agent you run, in one native Mac app.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.558
Otto feels at home on macOS: a grouped sidebar, one clean header per page,

4
00:00:12.558 --> 00:00:17.758
and Home as your desktop, showing what needs you, what's running, and what's next.

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.542
The floating bar is the front door.

6
00:00:20.672 --> 00:00:24.217
Press ⌘K, type or speak, and Otto runs the command,

7
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:26.661
or answers in one of four spaces.

8
00:00:26.791 --> 00:00:31.895
It docks into the status bar while you work, and ⌥Space calls it from anywhere on your Mac,

9
00:00:31.895 --> 00:00:34.682
with the menu bar and pop-out windows close by.

10
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:37.671
The Assistant is your personal agent.

11
00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:41.797
It keeps threads, remembers what matters, tracks tasks and reminders,

12
00:00:41.797 --> 00:00:44.322
and asks before anything leaves your Mac.

13
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:49.020
Agents run Claude Code, Codex or a shell as real sessions.

14
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.472
Keep them in tabs, tile them side by side,

15
00:00:51.472 --> 00:00:53.943
or work through a queue of what needs you.

16
00:00:54.073 --> 00:00:59.036
Broadcast one prompt to many agents, and pick up any past conversation from History.

17
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.330
Run with Otto turns a ticket or a message into a finished branch with one click,

18
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.766
and Mission Control shows the whole work graph: what's running, what's waiting, approvals and spend.

19
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.680
Then automate.

20
00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:15.359
A swarm gives agents roles, an org chart and a shared board.

21
00:01:15.489 --> 00:01:19.882
Goal loops plan, execute and evaluate until every acceptance check passes.

22
00:01:20.933 --> 00:01:24.674
Workflows chain agents, approvals and tools into pipelines.

23
00:01:24.804 --> 00:01:26.720
Scheduled tasks run on a cadence,

24
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.413
and personal agents keep their own soul, schedule and memory.

25
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.613
Git is built in: a commit graph with your work in progress, branches,

26
00:01:35.613 --> 00:01:39.969
pull requests, and multi-agent AI review with findings you can act on.

27
00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:42.883
Proof packs keep the evidence behind every change.

28
00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:46.411
Product turns stories into analysis and drafts,

29
00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:50.621
and the Vault keeps your docs as linked markdown with a live knowledge graph.

30
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:57.580
Design Hall brings every studio under one roof: frames, templates, Site Studio, brand kits and 3D,

31
00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:02.437
with references to earlier work and a log of what Otto learned from your team.

32
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.717
Skills Lab evaluates and sharpens your agent skills.

33
00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.791
Your infrastructure lives here too.

34
00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:14.854
The Database Explorer speaks MySQL, Postgres, MongoDB, Redis and ClickHouse.

35
00:02:14.984 --> 00:02:18.267
Build a query visually, with GROUP BY, HAVING and ORDER BY,

36
00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:22.756
then read the results in a grid, or one record at a time in the vertical view.

37
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.005
Connections hold SSH terminals and SFTP.

38
00:02:27.135 --> 00:02:32.930
Browse Kafka topics, AWS and Kubernetes, call APIs, read the web in the built-in browser,

39
00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:37.182
and govern every agent tool call through the MCP control plane.

40
00:02:38.233 --> 00:02:41.754
Insights turns your activity into reports with key findings,

41
00:02:41.754 --> 00:02:44.662
and Usage tracks tokens, cost and machine load.

42
00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.344
Snip anything on screen, bridge your agents to Slack and Telegram,

43
00:02:49.344 --> 00:02:51.205
and reach Otto from your phone.

44
00:02:51.335 --> 00:02:51.910
Otto.

45
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.982
All your agents, one home.
